  <qti-response-declaration identifier="RESPONSE" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-correct-response><qti-value>A</qti-value></qti-correct-response>
  </qti-response-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="SCORE" cardinality="single" base-type="float"><qti-default-value><qti-value>0</qti-value></qti-default-value></qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="FEEDBACK" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier"/>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-default-value><qti-value>show_interaction</qti-value></qti-default-value>
  </qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-item-body>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="show_interaction" outcome-identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" show-hide="show" class="qti-margin-0">
      <qti-content-body>
        <p>New members of the movement recite its ____ each morning; the handbook lists the twelve fixed principles and warns that questioning any one of them is grounds for expulsion.</p>
    <qti-choice-interaction response-identifier="RESPONSE" shuffle="true" max-choices="1">
      <qti-simple-choice identifier="A">dogma</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="B">consensus</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="C">propaganda</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="D">superstition</qti-simple-choice>
    </qti-choice-interaction>
      </qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>

    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-A" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Correct! Dogma means beliefs laid down by an authority as unquestionably true — twelve fixed principles, recited on command, with doubt itself punishable, is the word&apos;s textbook case.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-B" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! A consensus is an agreement a group reaches together, and it lasts only as long as the agreeing. These principles come down from above, fixed in a handbook and enforced — nobody arrived at them together.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-C" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Propaganda is messaging aimed outward, built to win over a public. These twelve principles bind the members themselves — an internal code recited at breakfast, not a campaign pointed at outsiders.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-D" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! A superstition is a folk belief about luck or unseen forces, held loosely and by nobody&apos;s order. These are codified principles enforced by an authority, in writing, on pain of expulsion.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
  </qti-item-body>
  <qti-response-processing>
